\begin{aligned}
{\left[A_{t}\right] }$ &=0.01 \\
t &=100 $\mathrm{ s}
\end{aligned}$1st order reaction,

\begin{aligned}$ k &=\frac{2303}{t} \log \frac{\left[A_{0}\right]}{\left[A_{t}\right]}\\
&=\frac{2303}{100} \log \frac{0.1}{0.01}=$0.02303 $\mathrm{ s}^{-1}
\end{aligned}$

For lst order reaction $\begin{aligned} k &=\frac{2303}{t} \log \frac{ \left[R_{0}\right]}{[R]}=\frac{2303}{40} \log \ left[\frac{0.1}{0.025}\right]\\
&=\frac{2303}{40} \times \log4=0.0347 \mathrm{ min}^{-1}
\end{aligned}$ Rate expression, $r=k[A]=0.0347 \times0.01=3.47 \times10^{-4} \mathrm{Mimin}^{-1}$.
